      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.8,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.3,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.1.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=0.8+0.3-2\\cdot 0.1=0.9.\n$$",
